{
  "id": "COMPOUND:29952 - PROTEIN:5782",
  "verbalization": "Citral, a compound found in oregano, is implicated in the interaction with DMS-273 through a multi-step mechanism involving protein tyrosine phosphatase LC-PTP. This enzyme is targeted by both Ginsenoside R10 and 5-Fluorouracil1-acetic acid hydrazide, which in turn target DMS-273. The presence of multiple pathways converging on the same target suggests a potential role for Citral in modulating the activity of LC-PTP, possibly through a common mechanism of action. The integration of these pathways highlights the involvement of protein tyrosine phosphatase inhibition as a key mechanism, which could influence cellular signaling and proliferation in DMS-273 cells. The evidence supports a plausible link between Citral and DMS-273, particularly through the inhibition of LC-PTP, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated.",
